{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_prediction_s90_item1_across_dl2_l3_across_dl2", "label": "L3-across dl=2 at the s->d collapse", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S90-ITEM1-ACROSS-DL2.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two routes are filed against each other so the clause cannot be rescued after the fact: path (a) a new phase-defect definition, path (b) two dl=1 trapezoids through the s's own p channel. If both hold (b) is preferred because it needs no new definition; if neither, L3-across dl=2 is written up as OPEN."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s90_item1_across_dl2_phase_defect", "label": "Phase defects delta_outer and delta_sc", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S90-ITEM1-ACROSS-DL2.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Measured against a Coulomb reference at the same E, L and region end-points so delta_outer vanishes exactly when q==1; delta_sc is checked against the banked delta = n - nu, with a looser 0.25 bar at two-well rows because barrier tunnelling is not in the action."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s90_item1_across_dl2_path_b_trapezoids", "label": "Path (b): two dl=1 trapezoids through the p channel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S90-ITEM1-ACROSS-DL2.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The filer's own expectation is weaker than the filed hypothesis: it should hold post-merge (38, 56) and fail by >0.5 at 37 and 55, because the p channel does not remove the two-well/merge discontinuity in g(l) at the d."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s90_item1_across_dl2_g_across_clause", "label": "G-across clause g(d) - g(s) < 1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S90-ITEM1-ACROSS-DL2.md", "source_location